1
00:00:03,038 --> 00:00:06,419
chapter 5.

2
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:10,960
As each day passed I would learn, in our

3
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:11,859
talk,

4
00:00:11,859 --> 00:00:14,200
something about the little prince's

5
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:17,500
planet, his departure from it and about

6
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,599
his journey.

7
00:00:19,599 --> 00:00:21,460
The information would come very slowly

8
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:22,900
following the course of the little

9
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:24,819
Prince's thoughts.

10
00:00:24,819 --> 00:00:26,980
It was in this way that I heard, on the

11
00:00:26,980 --> 00:00:28,659
third day,

12
00:00:28,659 --> 00:00:34,000
about the catastrophe of the baobabs.

13
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,700
This time, once again I had the sheep to

14
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:37,900
thank for it.

15
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:39,640
For suddenly the little prince asked me

16
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:43,659
as if seized by a grave doubt--

17
00:00:43,659 --> 00:00:47,940
"It is true is it not

18
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:52,058
the sheep eat little bushes?"

19
00:00:52,058 --> 00:00:55,619
"Yes, that is true

20
00:00:56,019 --> 00:00:58,659
I'm glad!"

21
00:00:58,659 --> 00:01:00,519
I did not understand why it was so

22
00:01:00,519 --> 00:01:02,440
important that sheep should eat little

23
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:04,179
bushes.

24
00:01:04,179 --> 00:01:07,000
But the little prince added:

25
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,400
"Then it follows that they also eat

26
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:11,798
baobabs?"

27
00:01:11,798 --> 00:01:14,440
I pointed out to the little prince that

28
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:17,319
baobabs were not little bushes, but, on

29
00:01:17,319 --> 00:01:21,400
the contrary, trees as tall as castles;

30
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:23,500
and that even if he took a whole herd of

31
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:25,960
elephants with him, the herd would not be

32
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:30,960
able to eat up one single baobab.

33
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:34,000
The Little Prince laughed at the idea of

34
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,099
a herd of elephants

35
00:01:36,099 --> 00:01:38,500
We would have to put them up on top of

36
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:39,460
one another

37
00:01:39,460 --> 00:01:41,619
he said.

38
00:01:41,619 --> 00:01:45,220
But he made a wise comment:

39
00:01:45,220 --> 00:01:47,798
"Before they grow so big

40
00:01:47,798 --> 00:01:52,179
baobabs start out by being little."

41
00:01:52,179 --> 00:01:55,599
"That is so very true I said.

42
00:01:55,599 --> 00:01:58,419
"But why do you want the sheep to eat the

43
00:01:58,419 --> 00:02:00,460
small baobabs?"

44
00:02:00,460 --> 00:02:04,079
He answered me at once

45
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:05,980
um

46
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:07,900
as if he was speaking of something that

47
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:09,940
was self-evident.

48
00:02:09,940 --> 00:02:12,279
And I was obliged to make a great mental

49
00:02:12,279 --> 00:02:14,380
effort to solve this problem, without any

50
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:15,940
assistance.

51
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:18,099
Indeed, as I learned,

52
00:02:18,099 --> 00:02:20,019
there were on the little Prince's Planet

53
00:02:20,019 --> 00:02:22,480
as on all planets--

54
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:25,960
good plants and bad plants.

55
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:28,659
In consequence, there were good seeds

56
00:02:28,659 --> 00:02:31,058
coming from good plants, and bad seeds

57
00:02:31,058 --> 00:02:32,619
from bad plants.

58
00:02:32,619 --> 00:02:35,919
But seeds are almost invisible.

59
00:02:35,919 --> 00:02:37,900
They sleep deep in the heart of the

60
00:02:37,900 --> 00:02:39,759
earth's darkness, until one of them

61
00:02:39,759 --> 00:02:42,279
suddenly decides to wake up

62
00:02:42,279 --> 00:02:45,099
Then this little seed stretches itself

63
00:02:45,099 --> 00:02:48,220
and begins timidly at first--

64
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:51,058
to push a charming little sprig

65
00:02:51,058 --> 00:02:55,119
inoffensively upward towards the sun.

66
00:02:55,119 --> 00:02:58,000
If it is only a sprout of radish or a

67
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,700
sprig of rose bush one would let it grow

68
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:02,619
wherever it might wish.

69
00:03:02,619 --> 00:03:06,279
But when it is a weed or a bad plant, one

70
00:03:06,279 --> 00:03:09,640
must root out and destroy it at once as

71
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:13,058
soon as it is so recognized

72
00:03:13,058 --> 00:03:15,240
foreign

73
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:19,419
terrible seeds on the little Prince's

74
00:03:19,419 --> 00:03:21,940
Planet these were the seeds of the

75
00:03:21,940 --> 00:03:23,259
baobab.

76
00:03:23,259 --> 00:03:25,659
The soil of that planet was infested

77
00:03:25,659 --> 00:03:26,679
with them

78
00:03:26,679 --> 00:03:28,480
but if you do not attend to this upper

79
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:31,480
routing in time you will never get rid

80
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:34,960
of a Baobab It spreads over the entire

81
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:36,220
planet

82
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:40,058
its strong roots bore clear through it

83
00:03:40,058 --> 00:03:42,759
And if the planet is too small, and if

84
00:03:42,759 --> 00:03:45,159
there are too many baobabs the planet

85
00:03:45,159 --> 00:03:49,980
May well split in pieces...

86
00:03:50,619 --> 00:03:54,159
"It is a question of discipline said the

87
00:03:54,159 --> 00:03:56,259
little prince to me later on.

88
00:03:56,259 --> 00:03:58,119
"When you have finished your own toilet

89
00:03:58,119 --> 00:04:00,759
in the morning it is time thereafter to

90
00:04:00,759 --> 00:04:03,519
attend to the planet's toilet just so,

91
00:04:03,519 --> 00:04:05,740
with the greatest care.

92
00:04:05,740 --> 00:04:07,778
You must see to it that you pull out the

93
00:04:07,778 --> 00:04:09,940
baobabs very regularly the moment they

94
00:04:09,940 --> 00:04:11,200
can be distinguished from the rose

95
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:13,538
bushes they resemble so closely in their

96
00:04:13,538 --> 00:04:15,099
earliest youth.

97
00:04:15,099 --> 00:04:19,480
It is very tedious work," the little

98
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:21,038
prince added,

99
00:04:21,038 --> 00:04:24,940
"but it is also very easy."

100
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:28,480
And one day he said to me:

101
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:31,058
"You ought to make a beautiful drawing, so

102
00:04:31,058 --> 00:04:32,679
that the children where you live can see

103
00:04:32,679 --> 00:04:35,079
exactly how all this is.

104
00:04:35,079 --> 00:04:37,000
That would be very useful to them if

105
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,859
they were to travel someday

106
00:04:38,859 --> 00:04:41,500
it may seem convenient Sometimes to put

107
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:43,839
off one's work until another day.

108
00:04:43,839 --> 00:04:47,038
But in the case of baobabs it would be

109
00:04:47,038 --> 00:04:49,538
catastrophic to do so

110
00:04:49,538 --> 00:04:51,880
I knew a planet that was inhabited by a

111
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:55,359
lazy man. He had neglected three little

112
00:04:55,359 --> 00:04:58,079
bushes..."

113
00:04:59,798 --> 00:05:02,740
So, as the little prince described it to

114
00:05:02,740 --> 00:05:06,579
me, I have made a drawing of that planet.

115
00:05:06,579 --> 00:05:08,919
I do not much wish to act like a

116
00:05:08,919 --> 00:05:11,558
moralist. But the danger of baobabs is so

117
00:05:11,558 --> 00:05:13,419
little understood, and the risks are so

118
00:05:13,419 --> 00:05:15,278
considerable to anyone who might get

119
00:05:15,278 --> 00:05:18,759
lost on an asteroid, that for once I am

120
00:05:18,759 --> 00:05:22,298
making an exception to my reserve.

121
00:05:22,298 --> 00:05:25,380
"Children," I say plainly,

122
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:29,740
"watch out for the baobabs!"

123
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:32,259
My friends, like myself, have been

124
00:05:32,259 --> 00:05:34,000
skirting this danger for a long time,

125
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,519
without ever knowing it; and so it is for

126
00:05:36,519 --> 00:05:39,159
them that I have worked so hard over

127
00:05:39,159 --> 00:05:40,659
this drawing.

128
00:05:40,659 --> 00:05:42,640
The lesson which I pass on by this means

129
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:45,819
is worth all the trouble it has cost me.

130
00:05:45,819 --> 00:05:48,099
Perhaps she will ask me,

131
00:05:48,099 --> 00:05:49,960
"Why there are no other drawings in this

132
00:05:49,960 --> 00:05:52,900
book is magnificent and impressive as

133
00:05:52,900 --> 00:05:55,419
the drawing of the baobabs?"

134
00:05:55,419 --> 00:05:57,819
The reply is quite simple.

135
00:05:57,819 --> 00:05:59,619
I have tried.

136
00:05:59,619 --> 00:06:01,599
But with the others I have not been

137
00:06:01,599 --> 00:06:03,038
successful.

138
00:06:03,038 --> 00:06:05,140
When I made the drawings of the baobabs

139
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:08,200
I was carried beyond myself by the

140
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:13,859
inspiring force of urgent necessity
